    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe Zig functional test harness starts the test runner with runtime and Lua search paths relative to the process working directory:\n\n```text\nVIMRUNTIME=runtime\n--helper=./test/functional/preload.lua\n--lpath=./src/?.lua\n--lpath=./runtime/lua/?.lua\n--lpath=./?.lua\n--default-path=./test/functional\n```\n\nFunctional tests that change the process working directory can then lose access to runtime files and Lua modules. This shows up as failures such as:\n\n```text\nmodule 'nvim.dir' not found\nUnknown function: netrw#Explore\n```\n\n_See the linked pr below and the failing ci in the second last commit._\n\nThis appears to be a Zig harness issue rather than a feature-specific issue. CMake-based functional jobs set `VIMRUNTIME` and source/runtime Lua paths with absolute paths, and also run from an `Xtest_xdg` work directory populated with source-tree links. The Zig harness currently does not mirror those path assumptions.\n\nThere are already Zig-specific skips for related cwd/runtime behavior, for example `vim.treesitter not found after chdir with build.zig` in `test/functional/treesitter/inspect_tree_spec.lua`.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nFrom a Neovim source checkout using the Zig build:\n\n```sh\nzig build -Doptimize=ReleaseSafe -Dinstall-path=/usr/ functionaltest -- test/functional/plugin/dir_spec.lua\n```\n\nThe affected cases are tests that change cwd and then depend on runtime/plugin discovery, such as directory browsing through `FileExplorer` or netrw fallback behavior.\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nZig functional tests should resolve Neovim runtime files, test helpers, and Lua modules independently of cwd changes made by an individual test, matching the CMake functional harness behavior.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nnightly\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nnixos\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty nightly\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nn/a\n\n### Installation\n\nbuilt from source with nix neovim nightly overlay",
